# VIDEO-EDITING — the SYSTEM is versioned here, the CONTENT is not.
#
# Tal, 2026-09-27: *"push the skills ... push everything besides the actual
# content. And the heavy stuff."*
#
# Git is a COPY, not a move: everything below still lives on the laptop. This
# repo exists so the part that took a year to get right survives the laptop.

# ----------------------------------------------------------- THE CONTENT
# Footage is replaceable (camera + Frame.io). The edit SPECS are not, and
# those are .json/.md, so they are kept.
FOOTAGE IN/
VIDEOS OUT/
assets/
# ...but `assets/` above also matches skill folders. The SFX library's
# CREDITS.md + manifest.json are the record of where every sound came from
# (Pixabay; REPOS.md). Keep that text; the .mp3s stay out via *.mp3 below.
!skills/tal-video-editor/assets/
system/public/footage/
system/projects/_build-scratch/
system/projects/_tmp-*/
**/proxies/
**/_previews/
**/_review/

*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.mkv
*.avi
*.webm
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aac

# ----------------------------------------------------------- SECRETS
# A key pushed here is compromised even if deleted a minute later, even in a
# private repo — it stays in the history and has to be rotated.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
token*.json
**/credentials.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------- HEAVY + REGENERABLE
# ~11 GB of this folder. All of it comes back from a single install command.
node_modules/
.venv/
.venv-*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/
**/.remotion/
**/chrome-headless-shell*/
*.onnx
*.bin
*.dll
*.lib
*.exe
*.pack
*.dic
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth

# ----------------------------------------------------------- OTHER PEOPLE'S REPOS
# Cloned here, restorable exactly from skills/toolbox/CLONES.md. Not
# redistributed through this repo.
system/vendor/
skills/toolbox/add-zooms/
skills/toolbox/clipify/
skills/toolbox/cut-video/
skills/toolbox/find-broll/
skills/toolbox/video-use/
skills/toolbox/youtube-clipper/
.agents/
skills/brag
skills/brag-slim

# ----------------------------------------------------------- noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ----------------------------------------------------------- found on the first staging pass
# .claude/skills is a JUNCTION to skills/ — git follows it and would commit
# every skill twice. skills/ is the real directory; this is only a pointer.
.claude/skills

# Frame.io discovery caches hold SIGNED ASSET URLS — 3,126 time-limited access
# tokens in discover-index.json alone. Regenerable with frameio-discover.mjs,
# and not safe to publish even privately.
system/projects/_frameio/cache/discover-index.json
system/projects/_frameio/cache/index-backup-*.json
system/projects/_frameio/cache/index/
system/projects/_frameio/cache/framing/
system/projects/_frameio/token*.json
system/projects/_frameio/credentials.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------- PEOPLE'S WORDS ARE CONTENT
# Interview transcripts are the people in the videos, unedited - including
# everything cut from the final film. GAZA-GUY-TRANSCRIPT.md alone names a
# man's birth identity, his home town in Gaza, his imprisonment there and his
# neighbours in Hamas leadership. Never in this repo, public or private.
system/projects/_frameio/*TRANSCRIPT*.md
system/projects/_frameio/cache/
**/transcripts/
**/translate/
**/diarize/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- FRAMES OF PEOPLE ARE CONTENT
# 2026-09-28: 308 stills of Roman (inspection strips, contact sheets) were pushed
# to this PUBLIC repo because the media rule listed video/audio extensions only.
# A frame of a person is content exactly as a video is. Nothing a project
# generates for inspection goes up.
system/projects/**/_look/
system/projects/**/contact/
system/projects/**/_review/
system/projects/**/preview/
system/projects/**/beats_*/
system/projects/**/tmp_*/
system/projects/**/*.jpg
system/projects/**/*.jpeg
system/projects/**/*.png
system/projects/**/*.webp
system/projects/_refs/
**/transcript.txt
**/transcripts/
